CAT = "s6Trading"; SEG = "TRD"
Q = [
('A customer wants to buy Class A fund shares. The price quoted for the purchase is the:',
 'Public offering price', ['Net asset value alone', 'Redemption price', 'Prior day\'s close'],
 'Front-load shares are bought at the public offering price, which is NAV plus the sales charge, computed after the order is received.'),
('Under Rule 5310, placing a third party between the customer and the best market is:',
 'Barred unless it benefits them', ['Required for every large order', 'Allowed for any business reason', 'Allowed if disclosed to them afterward'],
 'Rule 5310 bars interpositioning unless the firm can show the total cost or proceeds to the customer were better than without the third party.'),
('Which is a factor in judging best execution under Rule 5310?',
 'Size and type of the order', ['The rep\'s commission payout rate', 'The customer\'s age', 'The firm\'s advertising budget'],
 'Rule 5310 factors include the market\'s character, the size and type of transaction, the number of markets checked and how accessible the quotation is.'),
('Which item must appear on a customer order ticket?',
 'Account number', ['Customer\'s yearly income', 'Customer\'s birth date', 'Rep\'s home address'],
 'Order memoranda record the terms of the order, the account, and the times it was received and executed. Profile data belongs on the account record.'),
('An order memorandum must record the time the order was:',
 'Received and executed', ['Approved by compliance', 'Paid for in full', 'Settled at the clearing firm'],
 'SEC Rule 17a-3 requires the memorandum of each order to show the time of receipt and of execution or cancellation.'),
('Under Regulation T, a cash account purchase must be paid within the standard settlement cycle plus:',
 'Two business days', ['One business day', 'Five business days', 'Ten business days'],
 'Reg T\'s payment period is the number of business days in the standard settlement cycle plus two, so T+3 with T+1 settlement.'),
('A trade is reported to a customer at the wrong price. The customer is generally bound by:',
 'Actual execution price', ['Erroneous reported price', 'Day\'s closing price', 'Better of the two prices'],
 'An erroneous report does not change the trade. The customer is held to the price at which the order was actually executed.'),
('A trade booked to the wrong customer account is corrected by a:',
 'Cancel and rebill', ['Reversal of settlement', 'New account form', 'Journal to the rep'],
 'The wrong entry is canceled and the trade rebilled to the correct account, with documentation and supervisory approval.'),
('Under Rule 4513, records of written customer complaints must be kept for at least:',
 'Four years', ['Two years', 'Six years', 'One year'],
 'Rule 4513 requires each office of supervisory jurisdiction to keep a record of written complaints, with action taken, for at least four years.'),
('Statistical data on written customer complaints is reported to FINRA:',
 'Quarterly', ['Monthly', 'Annually', 'Only on request'],
 'Rule 4530(d) requires summary complaint data by the 15th day of the month after each calendar quarter.'),
('A firm learns a rep has been indicted for a felony. Under Rule 4530, it must report within:',
 '30 calendar days', ['Five business days', 'Sixty calendar days', '180 calendar days'],
 'Rule 4530(a) events, such as indictments, must be reported promptly and no later than 30 calendar days after the firm knows or should know.'),
('Which written customer complaint must be reported to FINRA as a Rule 4530(a) event?',
 'One alleging forgery', ['One about delays', 'One about high fees', 'One about a website'],
 'Rule 4530(a)(1)(B) requires reporting a written complaint alleging theft, misappropriation of funds or securities, or forgery.'),
('A large customer claim in FINRA arbitration is generally heard by:',
 'Three arbitrators', ['One FINRA staff member', 'A federal judge', 'A jury of six'],
 'Under the Customer Code, larger claims go to a panel of three arbitrators, while small claims may be decided by one arbitrator. Arbitrators are not FINRA staff or judges.'),
('Mediation under FINRA\'s Code of Mediation Procedure is:',
 'Voluntary and nonbinding', ['Required before arbitration', 'Binding once it starts', 'Decided by a panel vote'],
 'Mediation is a voluntary, informal process in which a mediator helps the parties settle. Nothing is imposed unless both agree.'),
('Under FINRA\'s Customer Code, a customer may require a member firm to arbitrate:',
 'Even without a signed agreement', ['Only if the firm agrees', 'Only after first suing in court', 'Only for claims under a set size'],
 'Rule 12200 requires arbitration when the customer requests it and the dispute arises from the member\'s business, whether or not a predispute agreement exists.'),
('Expunging customer dispute information from a rep\'s CRD record generally requires:',
 'Confirmation by a court', ['The customer\'s phone OK', 'A FINRA staff waiver', 'Five clean years'],
 'Rule 2080 requires an order from a court of competent jurisdiction, usually confirming an arbitration award that recommends expungement, before the information is removed.'),
('A claim is generally eligible for FINRA arbitration if filed within how long of the event?',
 'Six years', ['Two years', 'Three years', 'Ten years'],
 'Rule 12206 makes a claim ineligible when six years have passed from the occurrence or event giving rise to it.'),
('Disputes between a rep and their firm are generally arbitrated under the:',
 'Industry Code', ['Customer Code', 'Uniform Practice Code', 'Mediation Code'],
 'The 13000 series, the Code of Arbitration Procedure for Industry Disputes, covers disputes among members and associated persons.'),
('Open-end fund shares are always in distribution, so a firm generally may not:',
 'Sell them on margin', ['Hold them in street name', 'Redeem them at NAV', 'Accept dividend checks'],
 'Section 11(d)(1) of the Exchange Act bars extending credit on new issues a firm is distributing, and fund shares are continuously offered, so they cannot be bought on margin.'),
('On the ex-date of a cash dividend, which open order is NOT reduced under Rule 5330?',
 'Sell limit', ['Buy limit', 'Sell stop', 'Sell stop limit'],
 'Rule 5330 reduces orders placed below the market (buy limits, sell stops and sell stop limits) by the dividend. Sell limits and buy stops are above the market and are not changed.'),
]
